    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d606">

                <pb facs="0687" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg675"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.6363/799: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hayes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-22T18:00:00+02:00">April 22, 1943—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 23—4 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1042. Your 924, April 23 [<hi rendition="#italic">22?</hi>], 10 a.m. While I do
                    not feel now that we should delay furnishing aviation gasoline until concession
                    for airline granted, we might say at same time we agree to furnish it that we
                    expect facilities to be given for American airline to operate in Spain in
                    international service upon request. Are we interested in local passenger service
                    between Spain and Portugal or merely in trans-Atlantic passengers?</p>
                <p>I should like authority to sound out Foreign Office informally on general
                    subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hayes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
